  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(14, 10, 296)\n\n(8, 17, 353)\n\n**Logic:** Third no. = [(First no.)² + (Second no.)²]\n\n**(14, 10, 296) →**\n\n⇒ [(14)² + (10)²]\n\n⇒ (196 + 100) = 296\n\n**(8, 17, 353) →**\n\n⇒ [(8)2 + (17)2]\n\n⇒ (64 + 289) = 353\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1. **(29, 7, 690) →\n\n⇒ [(29)2 + (7)2]\n\n⇒ (841 + 49) = 890\n\n**2.** (18, 6, 576) →\n\n⇒ [(18)2 + (6)2]\n\n⇒ (324 + 36) = 360\n\n**3. (5, 13, 194) →**\n\n⇒ [(5)2 + (13)2]\n\n⇒ (25 + 169) = **194**\n\n**4.** (12, 3, 135) →\n\n⇒ [(12)2 + (3)2]\n\n⇒ (144 + 9) = 153\n\nHere, (5, 13, 194) shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (3)\".",
